---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="the bot has to be summoned" description="rate limits, webhooks, and dual auth paths. notes from wiring a bot into x.">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="font-mono text-xs text-faint mb-4">
      <a href="/writing" class="text-accent hover:underline">writing</a> <span class="text-faint">/</span> the-bot-has-to-be-summoned
    </div>

    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-normal animate-fade-up">the bot has to be summoned</h1>

    <div class="essay mt-10 animate-fade-up delay-1">
      <p>notes from wiring the hot take bot into twitter.</p>
      <p>the bot needs to be “summoned” before it can reply to a user. if not, you get rate limited on the reply. after that the bot is limited for 30 minutes to 2 hours.</p>
      <p>the activity api (oauth1) works as a webhook to get mentions of the bot, rather than polling. the x app login handles posting and liking on other people’s tweets. dual path.</p>
      <hr class="my-12 border-border" />
      <p>none of this is in the docs as one story. you find it by getting rate limited.</p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-spice">the platform teaches you its rules by punishing you first.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-6 border-t border-border">
      <a href="/writing" class="text-accent hover:underline">← back to writing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .essay p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
